    "narrative": "The Austin Waves\u2019 lineup today is headlined by **Gunnar Henderson**, who earns our highest efficiency score of 81.88. Facing Melton, **Gunnar Henderson** benefits from a massive 16% park adjustment and a significant platoon edge, making him the anchor of our 5x5 pursuit today. **Kyle Tucker** also presents as a premier start with a score of 70.48; despite the moderate 4.25 xERA of the opposing starter, his middle-of-the-order positioning and elite profile make him a core contributor. Meanwhile, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (65.00) remains a must-start at 1B, with his score bolstered by favorable park conditions and a strong xwOBA, proving that even against a competent arm like Keller, he is too impactful to sit.\n\nOur bench strategy focused on maximizing efficiency amidst a cluster of marginal projections. **Nasim Nunez** (55.68) narrowly edges out the rest of the fringe options for the final UTIL slot, primarily due to his utility in stealing bases\u2014our scarcest category\u2014and a favorable matchup against P\u00e9rez. The most difficult personnel decision involved **Miguel Vargas** (55.29) and **Andy Pages** (57.97); while both occupy the lower tier of our active starters, they were retained over potential alternatives due to their platoon advantages. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** was considered but ultimately benched, as his dynamic platoon penalty against the southpaw P\u00e9rez erased his efficiency gains, leaving him on the outside looking in. \n\nWe are monitoring the status of several key assets currently residing on the IL, specifically **Luis Robert Jr.**, **Jordan Westburg**, and **Jorge Polanco**, whose absences continue to condense our lineup flexibility. The Austin Waves must navigate these gaps while relying on the daily output of **Jackson Merrill** (61.54) and **Liam Hicks** (51.54). **Liam Hicks** is worth watching closely; his efficiency is heavily tied to his leadoff status, and any mid-game lineup adjustments could fluctuate his production. With **Brayan Rocchio** providing defensive stability at 44.69, we are leaning heavily on our top-tier hitters to compensate for the volatility in the lower half of the order.",
